Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] Shorten STGMCARD load/save panel duration

PS1 panel durations (~1239/1266 frames) match async memory-card wait.
On the port, flat MemCard* is memcpy and the engine still issues one
128-byte sector per frame (~78-80 sector-frames). With the PS1 constants
the bar crawls to ~6% then phase 2 (20 frames) snaps to 100%.

Override to 100 frames under PORT_HOST so phase 1 tracks real sector
work with a short readable fill. Phase-2 start(panel, 2, 0x14) is
unchanged. Flat-save flush policy is untouched.

--- a/include/menus/memory_card.h
+++ b/include/menus/memory_card.h
@@ -102,7 +102,12 @@
 #define SAVE_CHECKED 4
 
 /* The durations of the panels shown while loading and saving */
-#if VERSION_US
+#if PORT_HOST
+/* Flat MemCard* finishes ~78-80 sector-frames; PS1 used ~1240 for async
+   card wait. 100 frames ≈ sector work + readable fill; phase 2 still 20. */
+#define MEMCARD_LOAD_FRAMES 100
+#define MEMCARD_SAVE_FRAMES 100
+#elif VERSION_US
 #define MEMCARD_LOAD_FRAMES 1239
 #define MEMCARD_SAVE_FRAMES 1266
 #elif VERSION_EU
